ll consolidate the very minor physical micro-actions a bit, but keep the key states.\n\nActually, let me think one more time. The instructions say:\n\"交付前按原文顺序重读整章，分别检查：主角与配角行动、状态变化、认知变化、计划与承诺、关系与资源、规则与数值、条件与因果、否定、推测、误信、转述及来源。\"\n\n- 主角与配角行动: 沈北川's physical actions\n- 状态变化: standing → sitting, holding board → almost dropped, clenching teeth → released, short breath → long breath\n- 认知变化: hearing the message, reacting\n- 计划与承诺: none\n- 关系与资源: 登记板 (resource), 厢车门 (location), 泥 (environment)\n- 规则与数值: none\n- 条件与因果: hearing message → physical reaction (implied causal)\n- 否定: 没有立刻站起来\n- 推测: none\n- 误信: none\n- 转述及来源: 对讲机里传来 (the message source)\n\nI think my list is comprehensive. Let me also consider if I should add a fact about the relationship between the walkie-talkie message and 沈北川's reaction. The text doesn't explicitly say \"because of the message, he reacted\" but it's strongly implied. I could write it as a causal relationship, but the instruction is to not use常识 to add things. The text shows the sequence: walkie-talkie message → 沈北川's reaction, but doesn't explicitly state causation.\n\nI'll skip the explicit causal fact since it's not directly stated.\n\nLet me also consider: is 沈北川's prior state of clenching teeth important? \"一直咬紧的牙\" - this suggests he was clenching his teeth all along before. This is a state that existed before the chapter's current moment. Should I record it?\n\nThe fact is: 沈北川 had been clenching his teeth (prior to the message). Now he released them. \n\nI think \"把一直咬紧的牙松开\" captures both - that he was clenching and now released. The \"一直\" implies duration. I could split this into:\n- 沈北川之前一直咬紧牙 - 已发生 (prior state)\n- 沈北川松开牙 - 已发生 (current action)\n\nBut these are really part of the same event. I'll keep them combined as \"沈北川把一直咬紧的牙松开\" which captures both.\n\nOK, finalizing. Let me also reconsider whether I should include the fact that 沈北川 was standing by the truck door (厢车门). The text says \"他顺着厢车门沿坐到地上\" - he sat on the ground a