eed to escape them:\n\"对讲机里忽然传来一句\\\"货已经卸完\\\"\"\n\nIf they are Chinese quotation marks, no escaping needed.\n\nLooking at the raw text more carefully: \"对讲机里忽然传来一句\"货已经卸完\"\"\n\nThe way it's rendered, it looks like:\n- \" (opening Chinese quote) - actually this might be \" or \"\n- 对讲机里忽然传来一句\n- \" (opening Chinese quote) 货已经卸完 \" (closing Chinese quote)\n- \" (closing)\n\nHmm, I can't be 100% sure without seeing the raw bytes. Let me just use the text as shown and let the JSON handle it.\n\nActually, looking at the instructions for evidence: \"evidence 必须是当前章节中的连续逐字子串\". So I should copy the exact text.\n\nThe text is: \"对讲机里忽然传来一句\"货已经卸完\"\"\n\nIn JSON, I can write this as:\n\"evidence\": \"对讲机里忽然传来一句\"货已经卸完\"\"\n\nIf the quotes are ASCII, this would be invalid JSON. If they're Chinese, it's fine.\n\nLooking at typical Chinese novels, the quotes are usually Chinese: \"\" (U+201C) and \"\" (U+201D). Let me assume they are Chinese quotes.\n\nActually, looking at the rendered text in the prompt:\n\"对讲机里忽然传来一句\"货已经卸完\"\"\n\nThe characters look like ASCII \" and \". But the inner ones for the speech might be Chinese. Without seeing the raw bytes, I'll go with what looks right and let it parse.\n\nLet me just write the evidence as it appears and use proper JSON syntax:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"facts\": [\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"对讲机里传来一句「货已经卸完」\",\n      \"status\": \"已发生\",\n      \"evidence\": \"对讲机里忽然传来一句\\\"货已经卸完\\\"\",\n      \"speaker\": \"来源不明\"\n    },\n    ...\n  ]\n}\n```\n\nHmm, I think for safety, let me use the exact original text in evidence. If the quotes are Chinese, no escaping needed. If they cause JSON issues, the user can adjust.\n\nLet me finalize with the original text as evidence:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"facts\": [\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"对讲机里传来一句「货已经卸完」\",\n      \"status\": \"已发生\",\n      \"evidence\": \"对讲机里忽然传来一句\"货已经卸完\"\",\n      \"speaker\": \"来源不明\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"沈北川原本站得笔直\",\n      \"status\": \"已发生\",\n      \"evidence\": \